2-Week Execution Plan (Production-Grade Push)

Goal:
Move from "feature works" to production-grade/senior-level quality.

==================================================
Week 1 - Quality + Reliability Foundation
==================================================

Day 1 - Baseline + Scope Lock
- [ ] Freeze major feature changes for 2 weeks (except critical bugs)
- [ ] Define success metrics:
      - booking success rate
      - payment success rate
      - refund completion rate
      - API p95 latency
- [ ] Document KPI targets and scope in this file
Definition of done:
- [ ] KPI list is clear and agreed

Day 2 - Unit Tests for Booking Rules
- [ ] Add unit tests for table capacity rules
- [ ] Add unit tests for reservation cost calculation
- [ ] Add unit tests for cancellation cutoff (3-hour rule)
- [ ] Add unit tests for booking status transition guard logic
Definition of done:
- [ ] Unit test suite passes consistently

Day 3 - API Integration Tests
- [ ] Test GET /api/bookings/availability
- [ ] Test POST /api/bookings/create-checkout-session
- [ ] Test POST /api/bookings/:id/cancel
- [ ] Test admin actions (check-in, no-show, cancel)
- [ ] Add conflict test (same table/date/time)
Definition of done:
- [ ] Integration tests pass with seeded deterministic data

Day 4 - Webhook Idempotency Hardening
- [ ] Ensure duplicate Stripe webhook events are safe
- [ ] Persist processed event IDs or enforce idempotent updates
- [ ] Add duplicate webhook simulation test
Definition of done:
- [ ] Replayed webhook does not duplicate booking/refund side effects

Day 5 - Refund Reconciliation Job
- [ ] Implement job to scan refund_pending
- [ ] Retry Stripe refunds from failed/pending records
- [ ] Update DB status and send message notifications after retry
- [ ] Add manual trigger command/script
Definition of done:
- [ ] Pending refunds can be recovered automatically or by manual trigger

Day 6 - Load Test Baseline (k6)
- [ ] Create k6 script for availability endpoint
- [ ] Create k6 script for checkout-session endpoint
- [ ] Run normal load scenario
- [ ] Run burst scenario
- [ ] Run race condition scenario
Definition of done:
- [ ] Baseline report exists (p50/p95/p99, error rate, throughput)

Day 7 - Performance Tuning Pass
- [ ] Tune DB indexes/queries from load test findings
- [ ] Reduce heavy payloads in critical endpoints if needed
- [ ] Re-run load tests
Definition of done:
- [ ] Improved second report with measurable gains

==================================================
Week 2 - Ops, Security, and Deployment Maturity
==================================================

Day 8 - Structured Logging
- [ ] Add request-correlated logging with requestId
- [ ] Include userId, bookingId, sessionId in key logs
- [ ] Use consistent JSON log format
Definition of done:
- [ ] Can trace one booking flow across all services/log points

Day 9 - Monitoring + Alerts
- [ ] Add metrics:
      - booking attempts/success/fail
      - webhook processing duration
      - refund_pending backlog count
- [ ] Define alert thresholds for failures/backlog spikes
Definition of done:
- [ ] Dashboard + alert rules are active

Day 10 - Security Hardening
- [ ] Add rate limiting to auth/booking endpoints
- [ ] Add strict input validation on all new routes
- [ ] Tighten CORS and Helmet settings for production
Definition of done:
- [ ] Security checklist complete with no high-risk gaps

Day 11 - Admin Audit Trail
- [ ] Log admin booking actions (who/what/when)
- [ ] Include check-in/no-show/cancel/refund events
Definition of done:
- [ ] Audit history is queryable and complete

Day 12 - CI/CD Quality Gates
- [ ] Enforce lint in pipeline
- [ ] Enforce unit + integration tests in pipeline
- [ ] Enforce frontend build + backend checks in pipeline
- [ ] Block merge when checks fail
Definition of done:
- [ ] Pull requests cannot merge without green checks

Day 13 - Staging Verification
- [ ] Deploy to staging
- [ ] Run end-to-end checklist:
      - happy path booking
      - conflict + refund path
      - cancellation cutoff path
      - admin action flows
Definition of done:
- [ ] Staging sign-off complete

Day 14 - Release Readiness Wrap-up
- [ ] Create incident/rollback runbook
- [ ] Create refund reconciliation runbook
- [ ] Document architecture and known risks + mitigations
Definition of done:
- [ ] Release candidate package is ready

==================================================
